---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Careers"
  description="PromptDNS careers: no open roles today. We work with contractors and specialists - here's how to introduce yourself."
>
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 py-16">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-accent">Careers</p>
    <h1 class="font-display mt-3 text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-ink">Careers</h1>

    <div class="rich-text mt-8">
      <p>
        There are no open roles at PromptDNS right now. We're a small, independent operation and
        we work with contractors and specialists - email deliverability, DNS engineering, design -
        when the work calls for it.
      </p>
      <p>
        If you're good at DNS, email authentication, or technical writing and want to be
        considered for future work, introduce yourself through the
        <a href="/contact/" class="text-accent">contact page</a> with an example of something you
        built, fixed, or wrote. Speculative CVs with no specifics don't get replies; a paragraph
        about a deliverability problem you solved does.
      </p>
      <p>
        As monitoring grows into a product with accounts and billing, this page is where real
        openings will appear first.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
